{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2823241","formula":"C₁₀H₄O₁₀","hill":"C10H4O10","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":4.0,"O":10.0},"names":{"en":"Benzoquinonetetracarboxylic acid"},"descriptions":{"en":"In chemistry, 1,4-benzoquinonetetracarboxylic acid is an organic compound with formula C10H4O10, or (C6O2)(-(CO)OH)4, which can be viewed as deriving from para-benzoquinone C6H4O2 through replacement of the four hydrogen atoms by carboxyl functional groups -(CO)OH. By removal of four protons, the acid is expected to yield the anion C10O4−10, benzoquinonetetracarboxylate, which is one of the oxocarbon anions (consisting solely of oxygen and carbon). By loss of 1 through 3 protons, it forms the anions C10H3O−10, C10H2O2−10, and C10HO3−10, called respectively trihydrogen-, dihydrogen-, and hydrogenbenzoquinonetetracarboxylate. The same names are used for the corresponding esters."},"fame":10,"pubchemCid":350050,"mass":284.13,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1(=C(C(=O)C(=C(C1=O)C(=O)O)C(=O)O)C(=O)O)C(=O)O","inchikey":"DMCTUEIMZPODLV-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"3,6-dioxocyclohexa-1,4-diene-1,2,4,5-tetracarboxylic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"350050","atoms":24,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":2.65,"z":0.007,"el":"O"},{"x":0.0,"y":-2.651,"z":0.005,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.89,"y":1.683,"z":-1.311,"el":"O"},{"x":2.895,"y":1.682,"z":1.307,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.895,"y":-1.682,"z":1.308,"el":"O"},{"x":2.89,"y":-1.683,"z":-1.311,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.128,"y":1.829,"z":0.959,"el":"O"},{"x":3.124,"y":1.829,"z":-0.964,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.124,"y":-1.829,"z":-0.963,"el":"O"},{"x":3.128,"y":-1.829,"z":0.959,"el":"O"},{"x":1.289,"y":-0.671,"z":-0.005,"el":"C"},{"x":1.289,"y":0.671,"z":0.007,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.289,"y":-0.671,"z":0.007,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.289,"y":0.672,"z":-0.